Pre-Deployment LLM Security Audit Tool — Build Plan
Context
This is a greenfield project (the working folder is currently empty, not yet a git repo). The goal is a portfolio-grade tool that runs a structured, OWASP-Top-10-for-LLMs-aligned red-team battery against an LLM application and produces a pentest-style report, with an adaptive mutation loop as the technical differentiator. Target: functionally complete and published to GitHub by September 2026.

Decisions locked in with the user before planning:

Test target: no existing chatbot project was found on disk, so Stage 0 builds a small toy "customer support" chatbot as the authorized target (fully owned, safe to attack).
LLM provider: standardize on the Anthropic API for the target, the judge, and mutation generation. Use claude-sonnet-5 as the target/attacker-facing model and claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 for judge/mutation calls (cheap, fast, good enough for rubric grading — keeps a full run under ~$1-2).
Experience level: comfortable with Python, new to LLM APIs — so API key setup, SDK calls, and prompt/judge patterns are spelled out; general Python/env setup is kept brief.
Per the source description, only 6 of the 10 OWASP LLM categories are in scope for black-box prompting (LLM01, LLM02, LLM05, LLM06, LLM07, LLM09). LLM08 is skipped (no RAG target), LLM03/LLM04 are out of scope by nature (need training-data/dependency access), LLM10 is noted but not built as a load-test. This scoping decision goes in the README explicitly.
Timeline (9 weeks, today = 2026-07-15)
Functionally complete by end of August, with the first half of September reserved as buffer for the real audit run, polish, and publishing — so "by September" holds under either reading of the deadline.

